== Overview ==
Bioluminescence is the production and emission of light by a living organism. It is especially widespread in marine environments, where independent lineages have evolved light-producing systems for ecological functions such as signaling, prey attraction, predator avoidance, counterillumination, and defense.

Bioluminescence should be distinguished from fluorescence: bioluminescence generates light through a chemical reaction, while fluorescence re-emits absorbed light at a different wavelength.
